# The desktop app's build-time configuration.
#
# Deliberately separate from the repo root's .env.example, which documents what
# the SERVER reads. This app ships as a binary and never reads the server's
# environment, so nothing here belongs in the zod env schema or the compose
# passthrough, because putting it there would imply the server consumes it.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed VITE_ to client code, which is the
# mechanism that keeps a server secret from being accidentally bundled into a
# file every user can read. Never put a secret in this file.

# Where the server lives. Defaults to the local dev server when unset.
#   development: http://127.0.0.1:3000
#   production:  https://<your-duckdns-subdomain>.duckdns.org
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
